        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. 'Misguided' military operation: Trump’s appeal for Hormuz support draws no commitments from allies Middle East Issued on: 17/03/2026 - 17:30 Modified: 17/03/2026 - 17:38 Genie Godula is pleased to welcome Peter Trubowitz, Professor of International Relations and Director of the Phelan US Centre at the London School of Economics. According to Professor Trubowitz, what we are witnessing is a dynamic in which both sides are trying to expand the scope of the conflict in order to gain leverage. Iran has broadened the battlefield by targeting regional actors and threatening the maritime chokepoint. All the while, the United States is attempting, so far unsuccessfully, to draw Asian and European allies into the effort to secure Hormuz. Cubans abroad will be able to invest, own businesses on island 17/03/2026 Americas Lebanon: In the Bekaa Valley, a Christian village shelters displaced Shiite families 17/03/2026 Middle East Guy Poran urges international community to demand Israeli govt end settler violence in West Bank 17/03/2026 Middle East Ghassan Salamé urges Israel and international community to let Lebanon 'do its job more efficiently' 17/03/2026 Middle East China overlooks Trump's demands for Hormuz strait, calls for all sides to de-escalate 16/03/2026 Middle East Israeli campaign in Lebanon seeks to 'degrade' Hezbollah’s rocket, drone and missile capabilities 16/03/2026 Middle East 'Near universal refusal' - European leaders reject Trump's demand for Strait of Hormuz mission 16/03/2026 Middle East Iran's underground arsenal, decentralised military key to press on with strikes on Gulf states 16/03/2026 Middle East"
